WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.548
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.818 --> 00:09.691
Go back inside. See you at work.

3
00:14.246 --> 00:16.114
Mr. Dokgo Dal.

4
00:27.066 --> 00:30.822
Do you want to go on a date with me?

5
00:30.822 --> 00:32.558
A date?

6
00:34.114 --> 00:37.636
Did you fall for me?

7
00:39.034 --> 00:41.515
Huh! Seriously...

8
00:42.170 --> 00:44.490
Yeah, a little.

9
00:44.490 --> 00:46.228
So...

10
00:47.286 --> 00:49.089
you want to sleep with me?

11
00:51.986 --> 00:53.766
What?

12
00:55.274 --> 00:57.302
No...

13
00:57.302 --> 00:59.790
That's not what I meant.

14
00:59.790 --> 01:01.986
To me, that's what dating is.

15
01:01.986 --> 01:05.370
Having meals, going to coffee shops, taking walks,

16
01:05.370 --> 01:08.550
that's what dating means to me.

17
01:08.550 --> 01:12.338
Isn't that what we do at work every day?

18
01:12.338 --> 01:16.883
But what can I do? I don't go on dates with people I work with.

19
01:17.826 --> 01:21.714
Well, if you're still attracted to me after your contract ends,

20
01:21.714 --> 01:24.057
we can talk about it then.

21
01:26.898 --> 01:28.612
Good night!

22
01:32.962 --> 01:34.762
Huh!

23
01:40.114 --> 01:41.162
- Yeah. - Godal!

24
01:41.162 --> 01:42.794
Where are you? It blew up!

25
01:42.794 --> 01:45.314
Check the website right now! It's going crazy!

26
01:45.314 --> 01:48.015
Ms. Gong! This is huge!

27
01:50.942 --> 01:53.814
I was so nervous all weekend that the server might crash.

28
01:53.814 --> 01:57.198
Look at the surge in view counts. Isn't it crazy?

29
01:57.198 --> 01:58.794
Is this in real time?

30
01:58.794 --> 02:00.983
Yeah! It keeps going up, I'm telling you!

31
02:00.983 --> 02:03.354
There are surprisingly a lot of people looking for our offline stores too.

32
02:03.354 --> 02:06.022
Wow, should we start preparing for that now?

33
02:06.022 --> 02:09.334
But is this even possible in such a short time?

34
02:09.334 --> 02:13.130
It seems some influencer mentioned it on a live broadcast as a boyfriend gift.

35
02:13.130 --> 02:15.866
She said the scented candle was especially impressive.

36
02:15.866 --> 02:19.404
Right. People say it surprisingly plays a big part when setting the mood.

37
02:20.338 --> 02:22.091
Everyone!

38
02:22.091 --> 02:24.754
Let me add one more piece of good news.

39
02:24.754 --> 02:28.330
We got a contact from JC Investment!

40
02:28.330 --> 02:32.318
They want to meet the CEO!

41
03:41.986 --> 03:44.134
That day...

42
03:44.134 --> 03:47.614
I was just grateful,

43
03:47.614 --> 03:50.306
and wanted to treat you to a meal,

44
03:50.306 --> 03:51.682
that's all I meant.

45
03:51.682 --> 03:55.890
And besides, I usually fall easily for people all over the place!

46
03:55.890 --> 04:00.614
I came for coffee because I felt like it too...

47
04:00.614 --> 04:02.424
Well... I'm just saying!

48
04:12.378 --> 04:17.306
Are you free for lunch on Friday?

49
04:17.306 --> 04:19.134
Unbelievable...

50
04:20.198 --> 04:24.858
How will you ever show your face at work again?

51
04:24.858 --> 04:27.154
I don't even feel embarrassed anymore.

52
04:27.154 --> 04:30.058
I guess I'm getting used to the shame...

53
04:30.058 --> 04:34.030
Fri... Friday lunch?

54
04:34.030 --> 04:39.010
Well, I don't have any lunch plans, but...

55
04:39.010 --> 04:41.130
- What time? - Around 1:00 PM?

56
04:41.130 --> 04:42.839
1:00 PM works...

57
04:44.150 --> 04:49.342
- Where? - The other side chooses the place.

58
04:49.342 --> 04:51.070
Me?

59
04:51.070 --> 04:53.146
What do you like?

60
04:53.146 --> 04:55.066
JC will decide.

61
04:55.066 --> 04:59.174
They said there's something to discuss and want the marketer to join us too.

62
04:59.174 --> 05:01.434
That's fine, right?

63
05:01.434 --> 05:04.110
Sure. Sounds good.

64
05:05.306 --> 05:11.270
It's fine. That guy is probably used to acting like that anyway.

65
05:11.270 --> 05:13.203
That makes it even worse...

66
05:15.582 --> 05:19.459
The visitor count keeps climbing. Screenshot!

67
05:21.026 --> 05:23.246
- Happy? - Very!

68
05:23.246 --> 05:24.858
Honestly, I was a bit worried.

69
05:24.858 --> 05:27.054
It's our first time running a marketing project like this,

70
05:27.054 --> 05:29.502
but I didn't know it would turn out this well.

71
05:29.502 --> 05:32.458
As expected! The power of marketing!

72
05:32.458 --> 05:34.670
Well, I'll admit it got people talking.

73
05:34.670 --> 05:38.514
Should we recruit Ms. Yeon Su while we're at it? What do you think?

74
05:38.514 --> 05:40.390
- Stop the nonsense. - Why?

75
05:40.390 --> 05:42.918
She's great at her job, friendly, and tactful.

76
05:42.918 --> 05:45.360
And she's kind of cute sometimes.

77
05:46.206 --> 05:47.710
Cute, my foot.

78
05:47.710 --> 05:49.922
True, she's not your type.

79
05:49.922 --> 05:52.098
You like bold women.

80
05:52.098 --> 05:54.077
Gong Yeon Su is bold too.

81
05:56.114 --> 05:58.373
Gong Yeon Su is bold?

82
06:02.890 --> 06:05.110
You really have terrible judgment in people.

83
06:05.110 --> 06:09.092
Especially for women! Your taste in friends is your only good thing!

84
06:11.870 --> 06:15.765
I wonder what kind of men Ms. Yeon Su likes.

85
06:16.642 --> 06:22.063
If it's a delicate and affectionate style, Yoon Jio is the exact match...

86
06:23.130 --> 06:24.254
Whoa! You scared me...

87
06:24.254 --> 06:26.402
Why did he cut in without even turning on his blinker?

88
06:26.402 --> 06:29.704
Come on, don't mess around!

89
06:34.302 --> 06:35.614
[Seonghyeon Civil Service Exam Academy]

90
06:35.614 --> 06:38.147
[Episode 5]

91
06:42.443 --> 06:43.477
I'm exhausted.

92
06:43.477 --> 06:46.439
- Good job today. - Seriously, my knees hurt so much...

93
06:46.439 --> 06:48.330
- I know. - Seriously, my back...

94
06:48.330 --> 06:50.582
- Grab a late-night snack when you get home. - Yeah? What are you eating tonight?

95
06:50.582 --> 06:52.354
- Tonight... fried chicken? - Chicken?

96
06:52.354 --> 06:54.522
Kang Si Eun!

97
06:54.522 --> 06:56.314
You go ahead!

98
07:01.834 --> 07:03.638
What brings you here without calling?

99
07:03.638 --> 07:07.525
You have to answer your phone for me to tell you.

100
07:08.586 --> 07:12.190
I was worried. Why haven't you been answering?

101
07:12.190 --> 07:13.938
I was busy.

102
07:13.938 --> 07:15.722
What is it?

103
07:16.414 --> 07:18.598
Why are you acting like this all of a sudden?

104
07:18.598 --> 07:20.374
Nam Su,

105
07:21.474 --> 07:23.290
we need to talk.

106
07:34.550 --> 07:36.334
Let's get married first.

107
07:36.334 --> 07:39.602
No, let's meet your parents first, and then go see mine...

108
07:39.602 --> 07:43.937
I auditioned for Wonder Beat's official crew, and I passed...

109
07:46.046 --> 07:47.778
I decided to go.

110
07:47.778 --> 07:49.484
That's my answer.

111
07:50.698 --> 07:53.042
- Si Eun! - I'll call you soon.

112
07:53.042 --> 07:55.006
Accompany me as my guardian.

113
07:59.478 --> 08:02.582
How could you not even talk to me and just decide this on your own?

114
08:02.582 --> 08:05.866
Would talking change anything?

115
08:05.866 --> 08:07.558
It's my decision anyway.

116
08:07.558 --> 08:10.588
Is this just about you? This is about us.

117
08:11.642 --> 08:13.966
It's my life,

118
08:13.966 --> 08:15.726
and it's my body.

119
08:17.750 --> 08:20.334
You know better than anyone how hard I worked to get here.

120
08:20.334 --> 08:24.294
I gave everything for this dream. How can I just let it go?

121
08:24.294 --> 08:25.542
I can give mine up.

122
08:25.542 --> 08:28.522
I could drop my studies and even work on a construction site right now.

123
08:28.522 --> 08:30.726
For us, I could...

124
08:30.726 --> 08:33.222
I could throw my dream away!

125
08:33.222 --> 08:35.321
Do you know why you can do that?

126
08:36.442 --> 08:39.198
Because that was never your real dream.

127
08:39.198 --> 08:42.138
You might have lived your whole life without a backbone,

128
08:42.138 --> 08:43.968
but not me.

129
08:44.846 --> 08:46.678
I won't live like that.

130
09:10.722 --> 09:12.559
- Gong Yeon Su? - Uh... yeah...

131
09:14.398 --> 09:18.515
- Seung Jun? - Wow, holy crap...

132
09:19.386 --> 09:20.670
Have you... been well?

133
09:20.670 --> 09:25.006
Yeah. I've been... good. What about you?

134
09:25.006 --> 09:27.457
I've been doing well too.

135
09:29.598 --> 09:31.522
What brings you here?

136
09:31.522 --> 09:32.910
Oh, I have a meeting.

137
09:32.910 --> 09:36.216
A meeting? Me too...

138
09:41.522 --> 09:43.254
Wait!

139
09:48.346 --> 09:52.732
Don't tell me your meeting is...

140
10:02.758 --> 10:05.610
- I'm General Manager Jang Yu Jin. - Hello.

141
10:05.610 --> 10:07.890
And this is our...

142
10:07.890 --> 10:09.614
Oh.

143
10:09.614 --> 10:12.335
Marketing manager, Choi Seung Jun.

144
10:33.450 --> 10:36.150
We've thoroughly reviewed the proposal you sent us.

145
10:36.150 --> 10:37.958
I noticed the pop-up store will be located in Busan.

146
10:37.958 --> 10:42.214
Busan is our CEO's hometown, so he has a special fondness for it.

147
10:42.214 --> 10:44.954
We also plan to expand our chain business there later.

148
10:44.954 --> 10:48.658
Yes, and the CEO trusts our general manager so much

149
10:48.658 --> 10:51.146
that he put her in charge of the entire franchise.

150
10:51.146 --> 10:54.002
Oh, allow me.

151
10:55.778 --> 10:57.510
Thank you.

152
11:00.202 --> 11:04.614
By the way, as far as I know,

153
11:04.614 --> 11:07.506
this isn't really your style...

154
11:07.506 --> 11:10.826
You've mainly handled marketing with a wholesome image,

155
11:10.826 --> 11:13.855
like credit cards and banks, right?

156
11:14.514 --> 11:18.110
Well... yes...

157
11:19.022 --> 11:21.278
A good craftsman never blames his tools.

158
11:21.278 --> 11:24.202
Ms. Gong Yeon Su is such a skilled marketer,

159
11:24.202 --> 11:26.158
that she excels in any field.

160
11:26.158 --> 11:28.190
She moved people with Horizon,

161
11:28.190 --> 11:29.532
and as soon as she joined our company,

162
11:29.532 --> 11:31.926
she scored another hit with the mystery box.

163
11:31.926 --> 11:34.746
The mystery box was your idea, Ms. Gong Yeon Su?

164
11:34.746 --> 11:39.502
Yes. I truly learned from Ms. Gong

165
11:39.502 --> 11:42.906
that marketing isn't a battle of products, but a battle of perceptions.

166
11:42.906 --> 11:44.761
Ah...

167
11:57.034 --> 11:59.078
I had no idea.

168
11:59.078 --> 12:02.562
You've been evaluating me so highly?

169
12:02.562 --> 12:05.826
If you're uncomfortable, you don't have to attend future meetings.

170
12:05.826 --> 12:08.526
The VP is here, and... well, so am I.

171
12:08.526 --> 12:13.002
Not at all! I'm fully committed.

172
12:13.002 --> 12:16.209
I'll make sure this project is a total success.

173
12:17.742 --> 12:19.671
Oh! Here they come.

174
12:20.438 --> 12:22.398
It was a pleasure meeting you today.

175
12:22.398 --> 12:24.250
I look forward to working with you, Ms. Gong Yeon Su.

176
12:24.250 --> 12:26.066
I look forward to it too.

177
12:26.066 --> 12:29.082
- Mr. Dal, could you join me for a moment? - Oh, sure.

178
12:29.082 --> 12:32.854
Then, I'll see you later.

179
12:32.854 --> 12:35.353
- I'll wait outside too. - Okay.

180
12:40.210 --> 12:42.122
Hey, is this because of me?

181
12:42.122 --> 12:43.326
What? What did you say?

182
12:43.326 --> 12:46.278
Taking on a project like this isn't like you...

183
12:46.278 --> 12:48.606
Were you that shocked because of me?

184
12:48.606 --> 12:51.490
Or did you need a new change in your life? What is it, really?

185
12:51.490 --> 12:53.306
What on earth are you talking about?

186
12:53.306 --> 12:55.702
Even so, that guy is definitely wrong for you.

187
12:55.702 --> 12:57.346
He looks sketchy at first glance.

188
12:57.346 --> 12:58.646
Do you really have such poor judgment in people?

189
12:58.646 --> 12:59.954
Right?

190
12:59.954 --> 13:04.662
My judgment in people has been just terrible, hasn't it?

191
13:04.662 --> 13:05.982
No, I was just worried about...

192
13:05.982 --> 13:09.929
Shut up! Get lost.

193
13:12.186 --> 13:13.922
Ugh...

194
13:17.102 --> 13:20.916
Here's the product list for the Busan event. Here!

195
13:20.916 --> 13:22.198
Thank you!

196
13:22.198 --> 13:25.626
I was thinking of making the samples love gels and condoms.

197
13:25.626 --> 13:27.558
What about mini scented candles instead of love gels?

198
13:27.558 --> 13:29.170
People loved our scented candles!

199
13:29.170 --> 13:31.862
Giving them away as samples instead of selling them?

200
13:31.862 --> 13:34.412
He should never run a business.

201
13:35.346 --> 13:37.202
Let's do a pop-up limited edition!

202
13:37.202 --> 13:39.390
Limited edition?

203
13:39.390 --> 13:43.054
Colors, images, and scents that capture Busan!

204
13:43.054 --> 13:47.982
We use the ocean concept, redesign everything from packaging to copy,

205
13:47.982 --> 13:50.294
and do Mystery Box in Busan!

206
13:50.294 --> 13:51.778
What do you think, sir?

207
13:51.778 --> 13:56.374
Yeah. A pop-up limited edition could attract existing customers too. Sounds good.

208
13:56.374 --> 13:57.958
Nice! Sounds great!

209
13:57.958 --> 13:59.874
Love it!

210
14:00.538 --> 14:03.785
- Min Hyeong, book with the candle studio. - On it!

211
14:07.310 --> 14:10.910
There's an amazing samgyetang place nearby.

212
14:10.910 --> 14:12.306
Really? Have you been there?

213
14:12.306 --> 14:16.226
- Of course. It's a hidden date spot there. - Really?

214
14:16.226 --> 14:17.718
Hit the samgyetang place first,

215
14:17.718 --> 14:20.330
and then hit the coffee shop nearby with the amazing chai latte!

216
14:20.330 --> 14:23.022
- And right next to that-- - Meeting adjourned.

217
14:23.022 --> 14:25.196
Great work, everyone!

218
14:38.466 --> 14:41.729
[Sell My Items] 200-year-old traditional family soy sauce

219
15:02.790 --> 15:05.194
Do you know why you can do that?

220
15:05.194 --> 15:07.880
Because that was never your real dream.

221
15:10.630 --> 15:12.560
What do you mean?

222
15:16.042 --> 15:18.498
I want to quit studying

223
15:18.498 --> 15:20.786
and start...

224
15:20.786 --> 15:22.979
making money.

225
15:31.686 --> 15:33.146
Oh, dear...

226
15:33.146 --> 15:35.218
The soup is a bit salty today.

227
15:35.218 --> 15:38.990
I must have boiled it too long. Should I make a fresh pot?

228
15:38.990 --> 15:40.742
Never mind.

229
15:48.410 --> 15:50.631
Wow, is this lotus root?

230
15:53.594 --> 15:55.553
- Scorched rice water. - Oh...

231
16:09.402 --> 16:11.238
Make money.

232
16:11.238 --> 16:15.031
Pass the exam and become a civil servant first.

233
16:28.182 --> 16:30.129
Thank you for the meal.

234
16:33.562 --> 16:35.267
Good grief...

235
16:37.186 --> 16:40.126
Goodness...

236
16:40.126 --> 16:41.990
- I'll go check on him. - Okay.

237
16:41.990 --> 16:44.393
- Thank you for the meal. - Sure.

238
16:50.510 --> 16:52.923
[Shortest Pass Time, 3-Time Award Winner EduPang Civil Service Exam Pass! Free Pass]

239
17:09.122 --> 17:10.870
For two, please.

240
17:22.038 --> 17:23.974
Aren't you going to the academy?

241
17:24.766 --> 17:26.718
I am.

242
17:26.718 --> 17:28.205
The bus takes the long way.

243
17:28.205 --> 17:30.910
I know. That's why I'm taking it.

244
17:30.910 --> 17:34.894
Going to academy, study room, arriving home late at night.

245
17:34.894 --> 17:37.566
When else do I get to see daylight?

246
17:37.566 --> 17:40.346
Is that why you dropped a bombshell earlier?

247
17:40.346 --> 17:42.998
To see some daylight?

248
17:42.998 --> 17:45.198
If you're going to drop a bomb, do it properly.

249
17:45.198 --> 17:47.782
You just shot yourself in the foot again.

250
17:47.782 --> 17:49.516
How would I know when I've never done it?

251
17:49.516 --> 17:53.014
Must be nice for you, doing whatever you want in life.

252
17:53.014 --> 17:54.082
Me?

253
17:54.082 --> 17:56.132
Being a marketer was your dream.

254
17:57.318 --> 17:59.686
It was something I wanted to do,

255
17:59.686 --> 18:00.838
but not exactly a dream.

256
18:00.838 --> 18:02.526
What's the difference?

257
18:02.526 --> 18:07.206
It is different. What you want to do is about personal satisfaction,

258
18:07.206 --> 18:09.002
but a dream

259
18:09.002 --> 18:12.654
feels like your whole life depends on it.

260
18:12.654 --> 18:15.362
I wouldn't stake my life on marketing.

261
18:15.362 --> 18:19.071
Then what dream would you stake your life on?

262
18:22.626 --> 18:24.535
None of your business!

263
18:28.206 --> 18:30.686
I don't really know.

264
18:30.686 --> 18:34.253
What I should do, or if I even have a dream.

265
18:34.870 --> 18:36.597
Life just feels...

266
18:37.418 --> 18:39.458
like this bus.

267
18:40.090 --> 18:42.376
It goes round and round.

268
18:42.376 --> 18:45.364
Unable to get off except at designated stops...

269
18:49.002 --> 18:51.896
Would it have been a bit different if Dad was here?

270
19:06.954 --> 19:08.918
- Here. - What's this?

271
19:08.918 --> 19:11.248
Take it. I need to get off.

272
19:13.742 --> 19:18.255
Dad would've slipped you pocket money like this.

273
19:21.322 --> 19:23.658
Don't skip meals. Make sure you eat.

274
19:44.767 --> 19:47.193
[Under Maintenance]

275
19:50.926 --> 19:53.582
See you in front of the office by 10:00.

276
21:03.070 --> 21:04.090
[Electrical Inspection Notice: Due to power supply issues in Building 201,]

277
21:04.090 --> 21:05.997
[the elevator is out of service today. Please use the emergency stairs.]

278
21:05.997 --> 21:07.522
- Excuse me. - Yes?

279
21:07.522 --> 21:09.790
The lights in the stairwell aren't working...

280
21:09.790 --> 21:12.542
The whole line from Building 201 is like that.

281
21:12.542 --> 21:14.766
Ah... why is it acting up so much?

282
21:14.766 --> 21:16.550
Can it be fixed within today?

283
21:16.550 --> 21:20.085
Well, they said it would be fixed by 10 PM at the latest, so...

284
21:43.706 --> 21:47.266
Hey, Mr. Driver! To the candle studio, and make it quick!

285
21:47.266 --> 21:48.426
What?

286
21:48.426 --> 21:50.626
Mr. VP! You are coming with us today?

287
21:50.626 --> 21:52.470
The studio just called.

288
21:52.470 --> 21:54.582
The essential oils we ordered are running late.

289
21:54.582 --> 21:56.982
Really? Should we head out a bit later then?

290
21:56.982 --> 21:59.746
I figured, so I reserved a table at the samgyetang place.

291
21:59.746 --> 22:02.162
They say it's insanely good!

292
22:02.162 --> 22:05.422
All right, Driver Dal! Let's go!

293
22:10.682 --> 22:13.298
Can I put on some music?

294
22:13.298 --> 22:15.618
I like it quiet when I'm driving.

295
22:15.618 --> 22:17.851
Oh... okay.

296
22:19.682 --> 22:21.382
Let's listen to this together.

297
22:21.382 --> 22:24.233
Oh... thank you.

298
22:31.170 --> 22:32.766
- Wait, this is...! - You know this song, right?

299
22:32.766 --> 22:35.553
Of course! I love this song!

300
22:35.553 --> 22:38.530
At first, I thought the title wasn't "Nagging,"

301
22:38.530 --> 22:40.549
but "NAG-ging".

302
22:47.294 --> 22:48.441
Here it comes!

303
22:48.441 --> 22:49.526
Two, three!

304
22:49.526 --> 22:53.638
♪ Every single word is all for your own good ♪

305
22:53.638 --> 22:57.786
♪ To you who won't listen, it's just nagging ♪

306
22:57.786 --> 23:02.813
♪ Let's stop, let's stop ♪

307
23:23.126 --> 23:25.606
Mr. VP! You've got great taste!

308
23:25.606 --> 23:27.286
Of course!

309
23:27.286 --> 23:29.582
This song has to be a duet, you know?

310
23:29.582 --> 23:32.946
It has to be a duet! Let's sing it together at our company dinner later.

311
23:32.946 --> 23:34.762
Sounds great!

312
23:34.762 --> 23:36.972
Seriously, stop it...

313
23:40.286 --> 23:41.782
Enjoy your meal.

314
23:41.782 --> 23:45.306
This is lacquer tree chicken soup. Are you a leg person, Ms. Yeon Su?

315
23:45.306 --> 23:46.374
Well... I'm a breast meat person!

316
23:46.374 --> 23:49.510
Oh! I'm a leg person.

317
23:49.510 --> 23:52.378
Do you know that? White-and-yolk fatalism.

318
23:52.378 --> 23:54.758
What's that?

319
23:54.758 --> 23:58.290
People who like different things, like whites versus yolks, are meant to be.

320
23:58.290 --> 24:00.290
Since they can share it efficiently,

321
24:00.290 --> 24:02.798
they never fight over food.

322
24:02.798 --> 24:04.586
Oh...

323
24:04.586 --> 24:06.530
Actually, I just made that up.

324
24:06.530 --> 24:08.330
But it makes sense, right?

325
24:09.521 --> 24:12.382
It really does.

326
24:13.958 --> 24:16.474
That's just preference, not destiny.

327
24:16.474 --> 24:18.740
Not fate. You really care a lot about preferences,

328
24:18.740 --> 24:20.710
don't you, Mr. Dokgo Dal?

329
24:20.710 --> 24:23.966
People with picky tastes always obsess over preferences.

330
24:23.966 --> 24:27.650
So, what are your preferences, Mr. Dokgo Dal?

331
24:27.650 --> 24:31.351
Have you ever met someone you clicked with perfectly?

332
24:31.351 --> 24:34.050
In terms of personality, or sex?

333
24:34.050 --> 24:35.570
That's not what she meant!

334
24:35.570 --> 24:38.442
Relationship! She means have you ever dated someone?

335
24:38.442 --> 24:40.642
Well, if you count a one-day encounter as a relationship...

336
24:40.642 --> 24:45.032
A one-night stand isn't a relationship, strictly speaking.

337
24:45.032 --> 24:46.706
Everyone has different standards.

338
24:46.706 --> 24:50.074
The essence of a relationship isn't a momentary thing, but continuity.

339
24:50.074 --> 24:53.210
It must be based on continuous interest, affection, and responsibility.

340
24:53.210 --> 24:56.930
Relationships, dates, sex, marriage...

341
24:56.930 --> 24:59.422
You really love defining everything in life, don't you?

342
24:59.422 --> 25:03.834
These are all critical factors that determine life's major events,

343
25:03.834 --> 25:07.980
so of course you have to examine them thoroughly and exercise caution.

344
25:08.926 --> 25:14.611
How could a one-night stand ever be the starting point of a relationship?

345
25:15.602 --> 25:18.166
What are you, the head of the royal court inner quarters?

346
25:19.534 --> 25:22.026
But sometimes, doesn't a one-day encounter

347
25:22.026 --> 25:24.910
become the starting point of some relationship?

348
25:26.850 --> 25:30.298
Just like a good kiss can lead to asking someone out on a date?

349
25:30.298 --> 25:32.086
Huh!

350
25:34.550 --> 25:36.338
Well...

351
25:36.338 --> 25:38.890
All right, stop it, you two. Let's just eat.

352
25:38.890 --> 25:40.350
It's getting cold.

353
25:40.350 --> 25:42.781
Help yourself to the dry breast meat.

354
25:51.422 --> 25:55.722
No matter how I think about it, you seem like a total forever-single.

355
25:55.722 --> 25:57.602
Forever-single? Me?

356
25:57.602 --> 26:00.670
Someone who's never truly liked or loved anyone,

357
26:00.670 --> 26:03.498
an emotional, mental forever-single.

358
26:03.498 --> 26:06.142
You believe love is an illusion because you've never experienced it.

359
26:06.142 --> 26:08.262
You talk like someone with tons of romantic experience.

360
26:08.262 --> 26:11.978
I may not have dated a lot, but I believe in love,

361
26:11.978 --> 26:13.731
unlike a certain someone.

362
26:15.390 --> 26:19.538
Since humans are spiritual beings as well as physical beings,

363
26:19.538 --> 26:22.066
at least I am doing a proper job with one of the two,

364
26:22.066 --> 26:23.938
unlike a certain someone.

365
26:23.938 --> 26:24.998
Having fun?

366
26:24.998 --> 26:26.892
It's not boring.

367
26:40.886 --> 26:42.042
Are you okay?

368
26:42.042 --> 26:45.702
You know... I think something is wrong with me...

369
26:48.078 --> 26:50.942
Well... Don't worry, I'm fine!

370
26:50.942 --> 26:52.390
Really, don't worry about me.

371
26:52.390 --> 26:55.870
Are you going to be okay? We can reschedule the studio--

372
26:56.758 --> 26:57.994
What is it?

373
26:57.994 --> 27:02.974
Never mind that. Right now... do I look awful?

374
27:02.974 --> 27:05.264
- Awful! - Get going!

375
27:05.950 --> 27:07.710
Bye!

376
27:08.658 --> 27:11.452
Will he be okay going alone?

377
27:11.452 --> 27:13.986
Just in case, I gave the driver my number.

378
27:13.986 --> 27:15.908
Let's get to work.

379
27:57.014 --> 27:58.626
Sir.

380
27:58.626 --> 28:00.953
- Oh. - Ah.

381
28:04.130 --> 28:07.790
I picked out scents with the summer ocean vibe you requested.

382
28:07.790 --> 28:12.247
Here we have the ones with citrus, aquatic, and floral notes.

383
28:18.546 --> 28:22.002
This one has a slightly bitter note, but it's not lemon...

384
28:22.002 --> 28:24.546
- It's grapefruit. - Ah, grapefruit.

385
28:24.546 --> 28:25.942
Take your time looking.

386
28:25.942 --> 28:27.902
- Okay. - Thank you.

387
28:32.146 --> 28:33.982
The aquatic scent lingers nicely.

388
28:33.982 --> 28:37.338
It smells like flowers, and maybe green apples.

389
28:39.602 --> 28:43.682
Do you think Mr. VP has reached the hospital by now?

390
28:43.682 --> 28:46.194
Well, no news is good news.

391
28:46.194 --> 28:48.508
What time is it now?

392
28:52.118 --> 28:54.174
Oh no... What should we do?

393
28:54.174 --> 28:57.918
That's concentrated, so the smell won't come out easily...

394
29:23.058 --> 29:26.886
It's fine. It's not because of the smell.

395
29:26.886 --> 29:29.241
Oh... okay.

396
29:34.182 --> 29:36.622
Ms. Yeon Su, I'm feeling much better.

397
29:36.622 --> 29:39.178
Do my lips look awful?

398
29:39.178 --> 29:41.645
They look just like Tom Hardy's lips.

399
29:41.645 --> 29:44.105
Don't worry, it's sexy.

400
29:45.354 --> 29:46.854
Who is it?

401
29:46.854 --> 29:50.846
Oh, it's Mr. VP. He says he's feeling much better.

402
29:50.846 --> 29:52.190
Why didn't he text me?

403
29:52.190 --> 29:55.543
Anyway, it's a relief. He really scared me.

404
29:55.543 --> 30:00.147
It's fine. The same thing happened to him when feeding a stray cat once.

405
30:01.178 --> 30:03.275
He has a sun allergy too.

406
30:04.842 --> 30:07.698
Believe it or not, that guy is even more sensitive than me.

407
30:07.698 --> 30:09.673
Oh, I see.

408
30:15.962 --> 30:18.006
Tom Hardy?

409
30:19.374 --> 30:22.961
She always has such a charming way with words.

410
30:38.006 --> 30:40.270
Aren't you going inside?

411
30:41.222 --> 30:42.917
Yeah.

412
30:43.682 --> 30:45.470
We still have things to talk about,

413
30:45.470 --> 30:48.570
so let's finish over another cup of tea.

414
30:48.570 --> 30:50.330
Okay...

415
30:53.966 --> 30:55.969
I'm thinking of dividing the pop-up space into

416
30:55.969 --> 30:59.432
[Pop-up Floor Plan] experience, event zone, and product zones,

417
30:59.432 --> 31:01.934
but I'm not sure if there will be enough space.

418
31:01.934 --> 31:03.958
There should be plenty of space.

419
31:03.958 --> 31:05.922
Have you thought about the space concept?

420
31:05.922 --> 31:10.102
Yes, but I'd like to discuss it with JC side as well.

421
31:10.102 --> 31:12.770
Since there's the budget to consider.

422
31:12.770 --> 31:16.662
Then I guess you have to talk with Mr. Choi Seung Jun?

423
31:16.662 --> 31:20.402
Well... yes.

424
31:20.402 --> 31:22.604
He's the person in charge.

425
31:27.710 --> 31:32.430
Do you have somewhere to be? You've been checking the time...

426
31:32.430 --> 31:34.634
Not really.

427
31:34.634 --> 31:37.894
It's just that the elevator is under electrical inspection until 10 p.m.

428
31:37.894 --> 31:40.150
Oh...

429
31:40.150 --> 31:44.184
Then can't we take the emergency stairs?

430
31:55.554 --> 31:58.456
Ah, I get it...

431
32:06.326 --> 32:08.102
It's fine, go ahead.

432
32:08.102 --> 32:11.926
I can just wait a couple of hours.

433
32:11.926 --> 32:14.006
- Let's go up. - It's pretty high up.

434
32:14.006 --> 32:18.451
Come on, I have that much stamina.

435
32:26.268 --> 32:28.061
Try to keep up with me.

436
32:37.658 --> 32:41.784
Stairs are quite a workout.

437
32:41.784 --> 32:45.058
I've only ever lived in a hanok,

438
32:45.058 --> 32:50.625
so I'm really good at jumping over walls.

439
32:54.562 --> 32:56.394
But seriously,

440
32:56.394 --> 33:01.328
you never had a first love in elementary, middle, high school, or college?

441
33:02.786 --> 33:06.538
When we were young, Mansu who lived next door

442
33:06.538 --> 33:09.710
liked Chorong from the front house.

443
33:09.710 --> 33:11.574
Who's Mansu?

444
33:11.574 --> 33:14.610
A poodle. He was really cute.

445
33:25.010 --> 33:26.710
Good grief.

446
33:26.710 --> 33:30.666
Why do you live on such a high floor?

447
33:30.666 --> 33:35.512
This is totally... wow, this is a modern-day Rapunzel, seriously.

448
33:36.986 --> 33:38.854
- This way. - Whew...

449
33:38.854 --> 33:42.894
Wait, give me a second.

450
33:42.894 --> 33:44.678
Just a second.

451
33:46.230 --> 33:47.910
Take a deep breath.

452
33:47.910 --> 33:50.469
Just two more floors to go.

453
33:51.470 --> 33:53.180
Two floors...

454
33:54.018 --> 33:55.850
Ugh...

455
34:05.314 --> 34:07.538
Ah... ugh!

456
34:07.538 --> 34:10.278
Oh? What's wrong?

457
34:10.278 --> 34:13.825
- Your back again? - My back! My back!

458
34:15.698 --> 34:17.614
Get on my back first.

459
34:17.614 --> 34:20.922
No, it's fine! I'm okay.

460
34:20.922 --> 34:23.838
Do you want to walk down twenty floors alone, or go up two more with me?

461
34:23.838 --> 34:25.637
Twenty floors...

462
34:28.082 --> 34:30.342
I can do it...

463
34:30.342 --> 34:32.046
on my own.

464
34:33.918 --> 34:36.178
Ah... ouch!

465
34:36.178 --> 34:40.106
Come on, get on my back.

466
34:43.422 --> 34:46.441
Hold on right here.

467
34:47.758 --> 34:49.994
Just relax. You're heavier when you're tense.

468
34:50.602 --> 34:53.773
I'm sorry...

469
35:36.686 --> 35:38.594
Unbelievable...

470
35:40.426 --> 35:42.598
Drink up. I'll go take a shower.

471
35:42.598 --> 35:43.790
What?

472
35:43.790 --> 35:45.906
Ah...

473
35:45.906 --> 35:47.454
Oh...

474
35:47.454 --> 35:49.337
- Sure! - Okay.

475
36:14.626 --> 36:16.422
Yeah. How are you feeling?

476
36:16.422 --> 36:20.162
Much better! Whoever invented antihistamines deserves a Nobel Prize.

477
36:20.162 --> 36:22.206
- They probably got one. - Hmph!

478
36:22.206 --> 36:24.726
I bought some chicken, and I'm on my way to your place. Almost there.

479
36:24.726 --> 36:27.474
Why are you buying chicken again when you just had a relapse from chicken?

480
36:27.474 --> 36:31.122
The chicken is innocent! The lacquer is to blame. Got beer at home?

481
36:31.122 --> 36:33.234
Don't come. I'm tired. Hanging up.

482
36:33.234 --> 36:36.134
Wait, what? I'm already--

483
36:59.034 --> 37:01.559
Is he done?

484
37:05.358 --> 37:07.882
What's wrong with me?

485
37:09.538 --> 37:12.387
Huh? What's going on?

486
37:17.902 --> 37:20.169
I'm all better?

487
37:28.214 --> 37:30.038
Where are you going?

488
37:38.946 --> 37:40.746
What about your back?

489
37:41.510 --> 37:44.218
It's fine now, so right now...

490
37:44.218 --> 37:46.087
You're leaving now?

491
37:48.990 --> 37:50.898
That hurts my feelings.

492
37:50.898 --> 37:52.634
What?

493
37:53.734 --> 37:55.588
Want to take a shower?

494
37:56.578 --> 37:59.892
Right now? Here?

495
38:03.454 --> 38:05.390
Right here, right now...

496
38:19.286 --> 38:20.989
I can't...

497
38:21.790 --> 38:24.650
No, I shouldn't! No...

498
38:24.650 --> 38:26.482
No!

499
38:26.482 --> 38:27.880
Ms. Gong Yeon Su...

500
38:27.880 --> 38:29.706
Ms. Gong Yeon Su!

501
38:32.742 --> 38:34.577
Were you asleep?

502
38:41.610 --> 38:43.520
- A bit higher. - Here?

503
38:43.520 --> 38:45.846
Yes, but a little to the right...

504
38:45.846 --> 38:47.366
- Right here. - Ow!

505
38:47.366 --> 38:50.109
Yes, right there.

506
38:52.738 --> 38:54.660
Done.

507
38:54.660 --> 38:57.994
Oh... T-Thank you.

508
38:57.994 --> 39:00.094
How long has your back been like this?

509
39:00.094 --> 39:05.075
Oh... for a while.

510
39:06.882 --> 39:12.590
Honestly, my family holds memorial rites twenty-two times a year.

511
39:12.590 --> 39:16.294
When I was little, my dad would help my mom behind my grandpa's back

512
39:16.294 --> 39:20.915
making traditional pancakes and preparing the food,

513
39:21.526 --> 39:26.298
but after he passed away, I took his place.

514
39:26.298 --> 39:29.838
That's how it ended up like this.

515
39:34.702 --> 39:40.977
Jeez, my dad made the best shiitake mushroom pancakes.

516
39:41.686 --> 39:44.998
Usually, people carve a star on top of the mushroom,

517
39:44.998 --> 39:49.330
but he always carved one with a heart

518
39:49.330 --> 39:51.682
and gave it just to me.

519
39:55.618 --> 39:57.619
Sometimes,

520
39:58.398 --> 40:00.663
I miss that so much.

521
40:05.890 --> 40:09.139
You must have been close with your father.

522
40:09.822 --> 40:11.662
Yes.

523
40:11.662 --> 40:14.443
Very close...

524
40:20.614 --> 40:23.614
But why am I

525
40:23.614 --> 40:25.658
lying here like this,

526
40:25.658 --> 40:29.834
telling you all this? Seriously...

527
40:30.650 --> 40:32.542
Beats me.

528
40:32.542 --> 40:35.326
Why did I have to spill the essential oil

529
40:35.326 --> 40:38.451
and put you through all this trouble?

530
40:39.566 --> 40:42.497
What a mess of a day in so many ways.

531
40:45.170 --> 40:50.880
It wasn't that terrible, though.

532
40:59.546 --> 41:03.130
Today was nice, honestly...

533
41:03.130 --> 41:08.231
Having good food, drinking coffee, going to the park,

534
41:09.514 --> 41:13.294
and working out on the stairs at the end.

535
41:15.482 --> 41:19.238
Having meals, going to coffee shops, taking walks,

536
41:19.238 --> 41:22.328
that's what dating means to me.

537
41:23.142 --> 41:24.290
Is that so?

538
41:24.290 --> 41:26.262
You know,

539
41:26.262 --> 41:30.798
when I asked you out on a date,

540
41:30.798 --> 41:35.994
it wasn't just because of that kiss.

541
41:35.994 --> 41:38.434
I thought that going on a date with you

542
41:38.434 --> 41:41.570
might break me out of my shell

543
41:41.570 --> 41:44.354
and push me down a path

544
41:44.354 --> 41:47.228
I've never walked before.

545
41:51.678 --> 41:53.743
If that's the case,

546
41:54.826 --> 41:58.082
can we try the kind of date I mentioned?

547
41:58.082 --> 42:02.952
- What? - If what we did today was your kind of date,

548
42:03.602 --> 42:07.214
I was wondering if we could try mine.

549
42:07.214 --> 42:09.554
So... you want to sleep with me?

550
42:09.554 --> 42:12.587
To me, that's what dating is.

551
42:25.482 --> 42:27.536
I say chicken, you say... Ah!

552
42:27.536 --> 42:31.386
Whoa... Ms. Yeon Su?

553
42:31.386 --> 42:34.667
I have to... go home...

554
42:40.278 --> 42:42.034
Tsk!

555
42:48.026 --> 42:51.054
Speed bump ahead.

556
42:53.554 --> 42:56.422
You should've rested a bit longer before coming out...

557
42:56.422 --> 42:58.766
Shouldn't you go to the ER?

558
42:59.438 --> 43:00.550
Just go home...

559
43:00.550 --> 43:02.353
Just go home...

560
43:04.442 --> 43:09.102
Ms. Yeon Su, maybe this will distract you from the pain?

561
43:14.946 --> 43:16.758
Well...

562
43:16.758 --> 43:20.226
Please take the speed bumps more gently...

563
43:20.226 --> 43:22.258
Watch out for the speed bumps!

564
43:22.258 --> 43:25.009
Here it comes! Thump...!

565
43:32.018 --> 43:33.858
Good job!

566
43:45.942 --> 43:49.754
Really, I'm fine...

567
43:49.754 --> 43:52.645
Come on, let's get you home. I'll walk you.

568
43:53.690 --> 43:56.210
From here,

569
43:56.210 --> 44:00.002
I can go alone. I'm really okay.

570
44:04.854 --> 44:06.818
- Ah... ow! - Whoa!

571
44:06.818 --> 44:09.018
Doesn't look like it...

572
44:09.018 --> 44:13.165
I'm sorry... Could just one of you...

573
44:20.146 --> 44:23.710
Please help me to my door?

574
44:23.710 --> 44:26.694
Sure. I'll be right back.

575
44:26.694 --> 44:28.542
Huh?

576
44:28.542 --> 44:30.374
- Oh. - Give me your purse.

577
44:30.374 --> 44:33.202
Oh, thank you.

578
44:38.462 --> 44:40.544
I'm sorry.

579
44:40.544 --> 44:42.570
Nothing to be sorry about.

580
44:50.726 --> 44:53.514
What's your relationship with our Yeon Su?

581
44:55.022 --> 44:57.426
We're just coworkers!

582
44:57.426 --> 45:00.534
Oh, yes. We're coworkers.

583
45:00.534 --> 45:06.444
You have gentle, kind eyes... You must have a big heart.

584
45:07.410 --> 45:09.443
Oh, let me! I'll take that.

585
45:09.443 --> 45:11.174
Oh, okay...

586
45:11.174 --> 45:12.933
Wow!

587
45:24.846 --> 45:26.789
Close it.

588
45:30.190 --> 45:32.730
Where is your ancestral seat, Mr. Yoon Jio?

589
45:32.730 --> 45:34.902
I am the thirty-first generation of the Unjeong Yoon clan.

590
45:34.902 --> 45:39.458
- Unjeong... Isn't Unjeong Township in Gojin? - Ah, seriously!

591
45:39.458 --> 45:40.622
Yes, that's correct.

592
45:40.622 --> 45:42.582
And what about your family?

593
45:42.582 --> 45:44.322
I have my parents and three older sisters.

594
45:44.322 --> 45:46.522
I'm the youngest and the only son.

595
45:46.522 --> 45:49.395
Oh, my! What a blessed household.

596
45:50.026 --> 45:51.662
Do you perform ancestral rites?

597
45:51.662 --> 45:54.286
The head branch of the family conducts the rites separately.

598
45:54.286 --> 45:58.158
Sure, as they should.

599
46:01.798 --> 46:03.066
- This is scary... - From time immemorial...

600
46:03.066 --> 46:06.506
Only by honoring your parents and thanking your ancestors

601
46:06.506 --> 46:09.090
can good fortune bless your household.

602
46:09.090 --> 46:10.645
There are so many ill-bred folks these days

603
46:10.645 --> 46:13.969
who don't respect their parents or ancestors.

604
46:33.642 --> 46:35.441
Mr. Dokgo.

605
46:47.962 --> 46:51.282
Want me to call him and tell him to hurry out?

606
46:51.282 --> 46:54.535
No need. He'll be out soon.

607
46:59.550 --> 47:01.858
Do you usually come home at this hour after academy?

608
47:01.858 --> 47:04.326
Actually, I didn't go.

609
47:04.326 --> 47:06.334
I...

610
47:06.334 --> 47:08.674
I'm thinking of quitting studying.

611
47:09.842 --> 47:12.219
You're not going to marry my sister, right?

612
47:13.846 --> 47:16.265
You must have lied because you don't want to.

613
47:18.442 --> 47:20.830
You don't actually have azoospermia, do you?

614
47:20.830 --> 47:22.858
Since I spilled your secret,

615
47:22.858 --> 47:25.286
should I tell you one of mine?

616
47:25.286 --> 47:27.058
No need, really.

617
47:27.058 --> 47:28.877
My girlfriend...

618
47:30.506 --> 47:32.407
is pregnant.

619
47:35.286 --> 47:38.450
That's... something to celebrate, right?

620
47:38.450 --> 47:39.814
She says she's not keeping it.

621
47:39.814 --> 47:42.242
She said she can't give up her dream.

622
47:42.242 --> 47:44.402
I know it too,

623
47:44.402 --> 47:46.190
that dancing is everything to her.

624
47:46.190 --> 47:49.106
Oh, she's a dancer.

625
47:54.078 --> 47:56.864
I first saw her through the academy window.

626
48:04.274 --> 48:10.161
She was dripping with sweat, dancing with such a happy look on her face.

627
48:11.014 --> 48:12.818
She looked amazing.

628
48:15.166 --> 48:18.682
She had something I never had.

629
48:18.682 --> 48:21.247
That passion was what I fell for...

630
48:22.114 --> 48:25.000
Would crushing that make me too selfish?

631
48:27.266 --> 48:29.213
Honestly,

632
48:30.570 --> 48:32.402
I want to take responsibility...

633
48:32.402 --> 48:35.135
Why are you telling me this?

634
48:35.970 --> 48:38.347
Because I have no other guy to talk to.

635
48:39.534 --> 48:41.574
Whether to curse at me or cheer me on,

636
48:41.574 --> 48:45.479
there's no guy to give me advice from a man's perspective...

637
48:46.094 --> 48:48.366
But I thought you'd listen.

638
48:48.366 --> 48:50.658
Of course, if my dad was alive,

639
48:50.658 --> 48:53.253
he would've beaten me half to death.

640
48:59.058 --> 49:01.490
But I really don't know what to do.

641
49:01.490 --> 49:05.849
There's only one thing you must do, and one thing you can do.

642
49:08.878 --> 49:10.130
Respect.

643
49:10.130 --> 49:12.946
Whatever decision your girlfriend makes,

644
49:12.946 --> 49:16.986
you should respect and support it.

645
49:16.986 --> 49:19.763
That's your responsibility, Nam Su.

646
49:29.662 --> 49:31.634
Responsibility isn't complicated.

647
49:31.634 --> 49:35.206
What's more important to a man than being devoted to his family?

648
49:35.206 --> 49:38.650
The most basic things are often the hardest and most noble.

649
49:38.650 --> 49:41.346
Right, exactly.

650
49:47.678 --> 49:52.002
Tell me, do you plan on getting married?

651
49:53.610 --> 49:58.742
G-Grandpa? Why are you asking that?

652
50:02.026 --> 50:05.450
Wait, no, you shouldn't ask that...

653
50:06.450 --> 50:07.918
- Auntie? - Of course I do.

654
50:07.918 --> 50:09.962
Even if times have changed,

655
50:09.962 --> 50:13.150
- I believe everyone needs a life partner. - Of course.

656
50:13.150 --> 50:15.806
Building a life with the one you love,

657
50:15.806 --> 50:19.170
isn't that true happiness and our human calling?

658
50:19.170 --> 50:21.262
Well said!

659
50:22.994 --> 50:27.542
A harmonious marriage and a peaceful home lead to success outside.

660
50:27.542 --> 50:29.476
Absolutely! Harmony at home brings prosperity!

661
50:29.476 --> 50:31.518
Harmony at home brings prosperity!

662
50:36.618 --> 50:39.870
Take care! Come back for some makgeolli next time.

663
50:39.870 --> 50:41.666
Sounds great!

664
50:41.666 --> 50:45.042
Dear, let's cook another chicken soon.

665
50:45.042 --> 50:47.059
Okay, Mother.

666
50:48.046 --> 50:49.770
I'm back.

667
50:52.386 --> 50:54.358
Traitor...

668
50:55.886 --> 50:58.153
What are you talking about?

669
51:01.838 --> 51:05.206
I told you to go inside. You never listen.

670
51:05.206 --> 51:07.670
I'm fine. I feel much better.

671
51:07.670 --> 51:10.282
Are you all right too?

672
51:10.282 --> 51:14.253
Of course. One shot and it completely cleared up.

673
51:14.966 --> 51:18.026
Oh, I'm so sorry about today.

674
51:18.026 --> 51:20.166
My grandpa came out of nowhere...

675
51:20.166 --> 51:22.806
You don't need to apologize.

676
51:22.806 --> 51:24.438
I actually had a wonderful time.

677
51:24.438 --> 51:28.183
I got to drink dandelion tea and tour this historic house.

678
51:28.986 --> 51:31.370
It was fun.

679
51:31.370 --> 51:35.026
Seniors have always had a soft spot for me.

680
51:35.026 --> 51:39.054
No wonder my grandpa was chatting nonstop.

681
51:39.054 --> 51:41.138
I think he was totally charmed by me.

682
51:41.138 --> 51:45.354
Tell me about it. How could you give such textbook-perfect answers?

683
51:45.354 --> 51:47.286
Because that's just who I am.

684
51:53.254 --> 51:55.378
Ms. Yeon Su,

685
51:55.378 --> 51:58.102
what are you doing next weekend?

686
51:58.102 --> 51:59.586
Next weekend?

687
51:59.586 --> 52:03.761
If you're free, would you like to go on a date with me?

688
52:04.898 --> 52:10.392
We can grab a meal, have tea, and take a walk.

689
52:12.054 --> 52:13.926
What do you say?

690
52:15.586 --> 52:18.150
I really want to get to know you.

691
52:58.126 --> 53:01.193
If you need time to think...

692
53:01.898 --> 53:03.618
Let's do it!

693
53:08.226 --> 53:10.690
Let's go on a date.
